The bar's window list groups an app's windows, as the BeOS Deskbar does
(barlist.diff lists them one by one): the windows of one app other than
the focused one share one entry, at the first of them, with the app's
icon, or its short name if it has none, and how many there are, as
"st ×3". An app is a WM_CLASS instance, which tells Chrome's app windows
from Chrome's; its short name comes from the class, the last of its
dotted parts up to a dash, in lower case. A click on the entry focuses
the window of the group focused longest ago, so that clicks go round
them all. An agent waiting on you in one of them still shows, its icon
between arrows after the entry, as for a window of its own. The bar now
redraws when any shown window's chips change, not only the focused
one's. Applies after powerline.diff.

